WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.202
-Hey, everybody. Welcome to
"Tonight Show: At-Home Edition."

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.771
My name is Jimmy Fallon.
Thank you very much.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.872
It is Day 59 of quarantine.

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:09.375
59, I believe. That's the number
going out there.

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:10.610
So almost 60.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.678
Tomorrow's 60 days
in quarantine.

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:13.980
I'm staying at home.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.350
I'm wearing my mask
if I do go out, which is rare.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.251
I'm walking my dog.

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:22.421
My dog, Gary,
was faking a limp today.

00:00:22.421 --> 00:00:23.756
She was --

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.624
She didn't want to walk
as long as I wanted.

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:26.959
I go, "Gary, come on.

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:28.094
This is a thing."

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.329
She started, like, limping.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.732
I go, "Alright, no problem."

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.101
So, I try to walk her home
really slow,

00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:37.203
stopping all the way.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.871
Then once we got home,
running around

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:41.607
like nothing --
like nothing happened.

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.443
Let's get to some jokes here.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.944
Guys, if things
aren't crazy enough,

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:48.314
this weekend,
it snowed in New York City.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.649
We've been quarantined
for so long,

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.584
most New Yorkers woke up,
were like, "Holy crap!

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.786
I slept through the summer."

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.888
Yeah. What season is it?

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.557
Listen, I just saw
that across the country,

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.126
as states lifted restrictions,

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:03.295
several mini-golf courses
have reopened.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.998
But this is a little different.
You know at the end

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:07.800
when you have to get the ball
in the clown's mouth?

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.702
The clown's now wearing a mask.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.837
Very difficult.

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:13.605
Very difficult.

00:01:13.605 --> 00:01:14.907
Meanwhile,
Vladimir Putin announced

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:17.910
that restrictions in Russia
will be lifted tomorrow.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.079
That's right. Putin said now
that people can go back

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:24.651
to enjoying
all the old restrictions.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.120
Some entertainment news. I saw
that there's a television series

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.890
based on the "National Treasure"
movies coming to Disney Plus.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.725
And this is strange --
the Nicolas Cage role

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.395
will be played by Joe Exotic.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.365
Check this out.
7-Eleven has teamed up with Nike

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.601
to create a pair
of 7-Eleven sneakers.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.469
Take a look.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.038
And this is cool --
All the sneakers

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.374
are made from the same leather
as their hot dogs.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.512
They wait for it to rotate

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:56.983
probably a good 100,
120 rotations.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:02:00.052
Then they make the sneakers.

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:03.589
Listen to this. A rare type of
sea slug called the blue dragon

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:06.993
has been washing up
on a seashore in Texas.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.361
Is it me, or does "blue dragon"
sound like

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:13.800
knock-off male enhancement pills
that you get at a 7-Eleven?

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.002
Right next to the sneakers.

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:18.271
Well, once the pandemic's over,

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.907
I read that more workplaces
will go back to cubicles

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:24.043
and private offices
instead of open-floor plans.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.646
[ Fake crying ] That's too bad,
because I'm really gonna miss

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.983
hearing everyone's
hilarious ringtones.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.955
Ah, yeah. You're a fan of Lizzo.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.324
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.463
Oh, you're a fan of Lizzo, too.
Your ringtone's Lizzo.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:48.101
I get it. [ Chuckles ]

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.936
I heard that a lot
of grocery stores

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.772
are now limiting the amount
of meat you can buy.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.207
It's awkward when you try
to check out with too much,

00:02:55.207 --> 00:02:58.811
and the cashier's like, "We got
a meat hog at register five.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:03.482
We got a classic meat hog."

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:04.951
I read that some people
on dating apps

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.886
are trying to get their matches
to break social distancing rules

00:03:07.886 --> 00:03:10.657
and meet up.
And they're even trying out

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:12.825
some quarantine-themed pick-up
lines, too.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.293
I'll show you what I mean.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:18.131
For example, there is, "I just
tested negative for antibodies

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:22.301
but tested positive
for your body."

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.970
There's also, "Is that a testing
kit in your pocket?

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.506
Because I hope it is
a testing kit in your pocket.

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:30.309
There's a shortage of those."

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.578
And finally,
"I'm a Cuomo in the streets

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.147
and a Fauci in the sheets."

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.348
There you have it.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.417
That's the monologue
right there, everybody.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:39.218
Oh, my goodness.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.821
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.922
Multitalented guy.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.690
We're so happy to have him on
the show.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.191
Seth MacFarlane is here.

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:48.160 line:0%
This is his charity --

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:54.467 line:0%
peacocktv.com/forgood.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.402 line:0%
He's doing this
at-home variety series

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.704 line:0%
starting tonight
at 7:00 p.m. on Peacock.

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:00.939 line:0%
Check out what he's doing.
It's all for great causes.

00:04:00.939 --> 00:04:03.209 line:0%
So, we love having
Seth MacFarlane on the show.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.980 line:0%
Also on the show, founder of
the Momofuku restaurant group.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.183 line:0%
And he has a show, he's the
host, called "Ugly Delicious."

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.652 line:0%
My man David Chang
is on the show tonight.

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:15.388 line:0%
And here is his charity
that he's working with tonight

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:18.290 line:0%
to raise some money for the
restaurant workers out there.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.693 line:0%
And for musical guests tonight,
we have Lady Antebellum

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:23.595
who will be performing
"Champagne Night,"

00:04:23.595 --> 00:04:25.498
which is a song
that was composed

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:28.735
by one of the winners
of "Songland" on NBC.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:31.403
You know, during these times
in quarantine,

00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:33.172
I'm looking for anything
that can inspire me,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.708
whether it be from my wife
or something my kids say

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:39.111
or something I hear a bird chirp

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.514
or things I've seen
on Instagram.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:44.984
It's time for
"#Blessed #Inspired."

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.852
♪♪

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:53.526
-And now, "#Blessed #Inspired."

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:57.029
-Guys, we've been holed up in
this quarantine for a while now,

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:59.031
so we're looking for
any inspirational thoughts

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:00.800
or quotes or visions.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.269
And I know where to find them --
Instagram.

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:06.906
It's time for
"#Blessed #Inspired."

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:10.476
Our first inspirational
quote is...

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:13.178
"Your opinion of me
doesn't define who I am.

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:15.948
But if my pic of my homemade
sourdough doesn't get any likes,

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:18.584
do I even exist?"

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:22.154
[ Chimes ]

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:24.556
How about this morsel?

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:27.093
"Do one thing each day
that scares you.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.528
Unless it's catching a spider,

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:32.699
which my wife and I agreed
is really more her department."

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:35.034
'Cause I'm not touching
that thing.

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.368
[ Chuckling ] Ew.

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:39.339
[ Tibetan bowl chiming ]

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.210
Here's a treasure.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.013
"There's no saint
without a past,

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:49.682
no sinner without a future.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.051
And there's definitely
no Patriots without Tom Brady."

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.287
Oh, they ain't gonna
do it this year!

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:56.388
No way, Tom!

00:05:56.388 --> 00:06:00.625
Nuh-unh. Tompa Bay. Tompa Bay.

00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:02.194
Here's a spot of light

00:06:02.194 --> 00:06:04.363
sent through a prism
of a raindrop

00:06:04.363 --> 00:06:06.432
and refracted and "reflacted"

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:10.636
and reflected and refracted
in fractals.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:13.373
"Words can come back
to haunt you,

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:15.041
especially if you just
ate tuna salad

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.276
and you're wearing a face mask."

00:06:22.547 --> 00:06:26.285
[ Bowl chimes softly ]

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:29.921
Here's a bonus chunk of granola.

00:06:29.921 --> 00:06:32.758
"Be a voice, not an echo.

00:06:32.758 --> 00:06:34.493
Unless you're trying
to really annoy someone,

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:36.728
annoy someone, annoy someone."

00:06:36.728 --> 00:06:40.600
[ Chimes ]

00:06:43.769 --> 00:06:47.006
I see you!

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.674
See you over there!

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:52.578
[ Chuckles ]
This is a little blessing.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:55.047
"Some say that happiness
is a warm puppy,

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:58.885
but nobody says that happiness
is a room-temperature cat."

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:04.356
We're down to
our last gentle nugget.

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:07.459
"Help people even when you know
they can't help you back.

00:07:07.459 --> 00:07:10.062
Then keep reminding them about
that time you helped them.

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:12.665
They love that."

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:14.367
That's all we have time for

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:19.238
for this edition
of "#Blessed #Inspired."

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:21.140
Thank you very much.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:24.343
[ Tibetan bowl chimes ]

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:28.613
♪♪

00:07:28.613 --> 00:07:29.949
Oh, that guy --

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:32.118
That guy has it all figured out.

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:33.386
That guy's found peace.

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:35.053
Hey, you know what?
I want to check on some friends,

00:07:35.053 --> 00:07:36.222
'cause I miss my friends.

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:38.357
I miss my crew over at NBC.
I miss the Roots.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:41.994
So I got a chance to check in
with Tariq from the Roots today.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:45.798
And he just seemed a little
bothered, just a little irked.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:48.267
Check it out.
-♪ Tariq's Irk List ♪

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:52.137
♪ All the things
that irk Tariq ♪

00:07:52.137 --> 00:07:55.041
-Hey, Tariq! What's up, my man?!
How you doing?!

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:56.776
-Hey, what's up?
What's up, Jimmy?

00:07:56.776 --> 00:07:59.712
-[ Laughs ] You doing good, man?

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.346
-I'm good. I'm just
thinking of some stuff

00:08:01.346 --> 00:08:04.082
that I need to add
to my Irk List.

00:08:04.082 --> 00:08:06.351
-Your Irk List?

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:09.855
-Yeah, you know, like, my list
of things that irk me,

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:11.157
piss me off.

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:13.025
-What do you mean?
What's irking you?

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:15.694
What's bothering you?
-I mean, you know,

00:08:15.694 --> 00:08:19.332
I'm just tired of being talked
down to in my own home, Jimmy.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:21.400
-People in your house
are talking down to you?

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.968
-Yeah, exactly. Exactly, man.

00:08:22.968 --> 00:08:25.071
The wife, the toddler,

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:27.339
the teenager,
they all talk down to me.

00:08:27.339 --> 00:08:30.876
I mean, granted, they're all
taller than me, you know?

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:32.245
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:32.245 --> 00:08:34.680
That's cool. I'll give you that.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.348
-You're not that short, though.

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:39.518
-I'm not that short, but,
you know, just a little bit.

00:08:39.518 --> 00:08:42.020
You know, I just want to be
built up a little bit, man.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.922
You know?
-What are they doing to you?

00:08:43.922 --> 00:08:45.157
-They're too petty, man.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:47.392
It's like they take
all my favorite things,

00:08:47.392 --> 00:08:49.929
and they store them just
a little bit beyond my reach.

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:51.396
-[ Laughs ]
-Right?

00:08:51.396 --> 00:08:53.966
So, like it's to make me
think I can reach it

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:56.569
and then, you know, I try.
And then I realize I can't.

00:08:56.569 --> 00:08:58.971
And then it's like, "Oh, you
know, why don't you grow up?"

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:00.906
But I'm full grown.

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:02.975
[ Both laugh ]

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:04.276
It's like, I don't have,
you know,

00:09:04.276 --> 00:09:06.445
a retractable mechanical arm.

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:09.181
I don't have, like, a ladder,

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:10.949
a proper stepping stool,

00:09:10.949 --> 00:09:14.720
or a trampoline to pick up
snacks, you know?

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:15.821
[ Both laugh ]

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:17.356
-You're not Inspector Gadget.

00:09:17.356 --> 00:09:19.291
-Yeah, what I wind up
having to do

00:09:19.291 --> 00:09:22.928
is, like, risk life and limb
by climbing up on a stool.

00:09:22.928 --> 00:09:24.697
And then I get what I need.

00:09:24.697 --> 00:09:27.700
And then, like, to get back
down, it's more of an ordeal.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.302
I got to like, you know,
come down to one knee.

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:31.937
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:33.806
God forbid I jump off the stool.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:36.608
I mean, I could be
jumping to my doom. Nah.

00:09:36.608 --> 00:09:38.410
-This is stress
he does not need.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.912
This is stress you do not need.

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:42.014
-Exactly. It's too much, man.
It irks me.

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:43.915
My 4-year-old son Tariq,
you know Tariq.

00:09:43.915 --> 00:09:45.317
-Yeah, I love him.
-He can reach everything.

00:09:45.317 --> 00:09:46.385
He can reach everything,

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:48.988
no matter how high
we try to hide it.

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:50.422
-He's a cool dude.

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:53.425
-Last week,
I found a pile of wrappers

00:09:53.425 --> 00:09:56.495
and containers and stuff,
like, hidden in the cabinet

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:58.130
of all sorts of stuff, man --

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:03.602
gummies, snack bars, Go-GURTs,
random KIT KAT wrappers.

00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:05.137
[ Both laugh ]

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:06.371
It was a mess.

00:10:06.371 --> 00:10:09.208
And this is all stuff
that we keep on a shelf

00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:11.810
that's like 12 feet high.
You know what I'm saying?

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:13.745
I'm like,
how can you reach that?

00:10:13.745 --> 00:10:15.480
-Yeah, man.
-If you're that smart

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.249
and that self-sufficient,

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:19.852
you should be able
to wipe your own butt, right?

00:10:19.852 --> 00:10:22.388
-[ Laughs ]
-I mean, you should be.

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:23.955
But no. No.

00:10:23.955 --> 00:10:25.057
You know what I'm saying?

00:10:25.057 --> 00:10:26.759
I feel like he probably can,

00:10:26.759 --> 00:10:29.795
but he'd just rather, you know,
like, call for the royal wiper,

00:10:29.795 --> 00:10:32.264
like Prince Akeem
in "Coming to America."

00:10:32.264 --> 00:10:33.466
And then, you know --
-Why not?

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:35.100
-Exactly. Then here I come.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.203
-He knows what he can do
and what he can't.

00:10:37.203 --> 00:10:39.238
-Yeah, it irks me, man.
It irks me.

00:10:39.238 --> 00:10:41.006
[ Both laugh ]

00:10:41.006 --> 00:10:42.541
You know what else irks me?

00:10:42.541 --> 00:10:43.609
-What?

00:10:43.609 --> 00:10:46.078
-You know, talkative
tooth brushers.

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:47.346
-Talkative tooth brushers?

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:48.780
-Yeah, it's like my wife, man.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.783
I feel like, if it's something
pressing you that much

00:10:51.783 --> 00:10:53.719
that you have to tell me
right now,

00:10:53.719 --> 00:10:55.787
don't wait until
you're brushing your teeth.

00:10:55.787 --> 00:10:57.155
The electric toothbrush
is going.

00:10:57.155 --> 00:10:59.591
The water's going and stuff.
And then, you know --

00:10:59.591 --> 00:11:01.894
[ Mumbling indistinctly ]

00:11:01.894 --> 00:11:03.996
-[ Laughs ]

00:11:03.996 --> 00:11:05.965
I don't unders-- It's like
you're speaking in Morse code.

00:11:05.965 --> 00:11:08.166
I don't understand that.
-That is insane.

00:11:08.166 --> 00:11:10.535
-And then, you know,
she spits out the toothpaste,

00:11:10.535 --> 00:11:13.472
and it's like, "What time
did you leave us last night?"

00:11:13.472 --> 00:11:16.007
And I'm like, "What do you mean,
what time did I leave you?

00:11:16.007 --> 00:11:18.677
Like, I'm still --
I didn't abandon my family.

00:11:18.677 --> 00:11:21.212
Like, I awakened,
and I left the room.

00:11:21.212 --> 00:11:23.582
I started my day. Like,
what time did I leave you?"

00:11:23.582 --> 00:11:25.685
And then, you know,
when I leave the room --

00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:28.320
Actually, she's never,
like, bothered --

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.889
She's never worried about
what time anything happens

00:11:30.889 --> 00:11:32.457
unless it's my time.

00:11:32.457 --> 00:11:35.194
Like, when it's her time,
she's allergic to time.

00:11:35.194 --> 00:11:37.563
But if it's me, it's like,
"What time did you wake up?

00:11:37.563 --> 00:11:39.532
What time did you leave?
What time is the show today?

00:11:39.532 --> 00:11:40.799
What time do you guys get done?"

00:11:40.799 --> 00:11:43.301
Like, you know, what time?
What time? What time?

00:11:43.301 --> 00:11:46.705
But if we have to be somewhere,
say, at 5:30,

00:11:46.705 --> 00:11:48.573
we're leaving the house at 5:45.

00:11:48.573 --> 00:11:49.808
You know what I'm saying?

00:11:49.808 --> 00:11:51.010
[ Both laugh ]

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.711
And it's like, come on, man.

00:11:52.711 --> 00:11:55.147
Like, she's allergic to time
otherwise.

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:56.248
I don't know, man.

00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:57.950
It's crazy. Crazy.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.753
You know, I mean, like me,
I'm never late for anything.

00:12:00.753 --> 00:12:02.054
I'm always on time.
And you know that.

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:04.123
You know that, right?
I'm always on time.

00:12:04.123 --> 00:12:08.193
I pride myself in being,
you know, early even, right?

00:12:08.193 --> 00:12:11.897
-Sometimes you're -- Sometimes
you've been late for work.

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:15.934
-When I'm late for work, Jimmy,
that's on purpose.

00:12:15.934 --> 00:12:18.237
-Tariq, it is great
catching up with you, my man.

00:12:18.237 --> 00:12:20.873
Try to stay less irked,
okay, my friend?

00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:22.808
-[ Scoffs ] I'll try.
I don't know.

00:12:22.808 --> 00:12:24.243
-[ Laughs ]

